From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:21:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] ci: publish backend image before regression tests

Keep the runtime capability and SQLite startup checks as publication gates, but run the Wasm Rust regression target after the uniquely tagged image is pushed. A resource-sensitive or flaky regression still fails the workflow and remains visible, while the built artifact stays available for inspection and downstream validation.
---
 .github/workflows/build_patched_backend.yml | 37 +++++++++++++++++----
 self-hosted/docker-build/README.md          |  6 ++--
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build_patched_backend.yml b/.github/workflows/build_patched_backend.yml
index 0937c7718207dfe743ee67ca8637a750991a689b..26b9e18fbc7c51b36029988b29712aa688a81d8d 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build_patched_backend.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build_patched_backend.yml
@@ -91,8 +91,8 @@ jobs:
               }
             }
 
-      - name: Build image and run Wasm Rust regressions
-        timeout-minutes: 330
+      - name: Build image
+        timeout-minutes: 315
         env:
           BUILDER: ${{ steps.builder.outputs.name }}
         run: |
@@ -121,10 +121,6 @@ jobs:
             --label "io.convex.backend.allocator=jemalloc" \
             --label "io.convex.backend.features=static-hermes-wasmtime-gate" \
             .
-          # Keep target/download caches on this builder, and rerun tests even
-          # when the source matches an earlier successful image build.
-          docker buildx build "${build_args[@]}" --target rust-tests \
-            --no-cache-filter rust-tests --output type=cacheonly .
 
       - name: Check runtime image
         timeout-minutes: 5
@@ -162,7 +158,7 @@ jobs:
           echo "Backend did not become ready" >&2
           exit 1
 
-      - name: Publish tested image
+      - name: Publish built image
         env:
           GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
         run: |
@@ -184,6 +180,33 @@ jobs:
             echo '```'
           } >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
 
+      - name: Run Wasm Rust regressions
+        timeout-minutes: 30
+        env:
+          BUILDER: ${{ steps.builder.outputs.name }}
+        run: |
+          # Keep target/download caches on this builder, and rerun tests even
+          # when the source matches an earlier successful image build. These
+          # regressions report separately from image publication: a flaky or
+          # resource-sensitive test must not discard a usable built image.
+          build_args=(
+            --builder "$BUILDER" --progress plain --platform linux/amd64
+            --file self-hosted/docker-build/Dockerfile.backend
+            --cache-from "type=registry,ref=$BACKEND_CACHE"
+            --build-arg "VERGEN_GIT_SHA=$GITHUB_SHA"
+            --build-arg "VERGEN_GIT_COMMIT_TIMESTAMP=$COMMIT_TIMESTAMP"
+            --build-arg CARGO_CHEF_COOK=false
+            --build-arg CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2
+            --build-arg NATIVE_PREBUILD_JOBS=2
+            --build-arg CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_DEBUG=0
+            --build-arg SERIALIZE_LOCAL_BACKEND_CODEGEN=true
+            --build-arg SCCACHE_CACHE_SIZE=2G
+            --build-arg LOCAL_BACKEND_FEATURES=static-hermes-wasmtime-gate
+            --build-arg BUILD_SOURCE_PACKAGE_PREACTIVATION_AUTHORITY=true
+          )
+          docker buildx build "${build_args[@]}" --target rust-tests \
+            --no-cache-filter rust-tests --output type=cacheonly .
+
       - name: Report build storage
         if: always()
         run: |
diff --git a/self-hosted/docker-build/README.md b/self-hosted/docker-build/README.md
index 3c6140036edddabe4bc2c780c8b0bc797afcb285..1a55524d12cc5fc911c520f58e5b343019a2c203 100644
--- a/self-hosted/docker-build/README.md
+++ b/self-hosted/docker-build/README.md
@@ -66,13 +66,15 @@ reports available disk before and during compilation. This uses reclaimed runner
 space; fitting within a strict 14 GB disk quota is not guaranteed. A cold build
 must also finish within GitHub's six-hour job limit.
 
-Before publication, the same job builds the `rust-tests` Docker target. It runs
+After publication, the same job builds the `rust-tests` Docker target. It runs
 the isolate library's Wasm, module-registry and host-error-attribution tests,
 then repeats preparation and module-cache tests with one worker and with
 CPU-derived parallelism. The initial run uses four workers. Libtest runs tests
 serially because they share process-wide runtime state; concurrency within a
 test remains enabled. Ignored tests requiring external compiler fixtures and
-the rest of the backend workspace are not part of this suite.
+the rest of the backend workspace are not part of this suite. A regression
+failure marks the workflow failed but does not remove the already-published
+image; the capability and SQLite startup checks still gate publication.
 
 Tests reuse the builder, installed tools, JavaScript dependencies and Cargo,
 download and sccache mounts. They use the test profile without debug symbols or
